    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Formulas Used\n\n### Belt Length\n**lb = (dm × π / 2) + (df × π / 2) + (2 × lfm) + ((df - dm)² / (4 × lfm))**\n\n### Belt Velocity\n**vb = π × dm × nm / 60000** (metric units, m/s)\n\n### Belt Gearing\n**nf = nm × dm / df**\n\n### Horsepower\n**From Tension:** Php = Fb × vb / 33000\n\n**From Torque:** Php = T × n / 5252\n\n### Speed Ratio\n**SR = nf / ns** (where nf is faster and ns is slower)"
    }
